## Probit Model

$$p=\Phi(\beta_1+\beta_2x); \Phi(x) = \int_{-\infty}^x \frac{e^{-\frac{y^2}{2}}}{\sqrt{2\pi}}dy$$

### Likelihood function

#### Likelihood for logit model

$$L = \prod_{j=1}^k\binom{n_j}{n_j^1}\Phi(x_j\beta)^{n^1_j}(1 - \Phi(x_j\beta))^{n^0_j}$$

#### Log-Likelihood (removing binomial coefficient)

$$l((n^1_j|x_j)_j;\beta) = \sum_{j=1}^k (n^1_jlog(\Phi(x_j\beta)) + n^0_jlog(1- \Phi(x_j\beta)))$$

$$l((n^1_j|x_j)_j;\beta) = \sum_{j=1}^k (n^1_jlog(\int_0^{\beta_0 + \beta_1x_j}\frac{e^{-\frac{x^2}{2}}}{\sqrt{2\pi}}dx) + n^0_jlog(1- \int_0^{\beta_0 + \beta_1x_j}\frac{e^{-\frac{x^2}{2}}}{\sqrt{2\pi}}dx))$$

### Score and Fisher Information

#### Score Vector U

$$U(\beta) = \sum_{j=1}^k( \phi(x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{\Phi(x_j\beta)} - \frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}),x_j\phi(x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{\Phi(x_j\beta)} - \frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))})) $$

#### Fisher Information

$$I(\beta) =  \mathbf{E}[\begin{bmatrix} \sum_{j=1}^k \phi(x_j\beta)((x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{\Phi(x_j\beta)}-\frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}) + \phi(x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{(\Phi(x_j\beta))^2}+\frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))^2}))& \sum_{j=1}^k x_j\phi(x_j\beta)((x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{\Phi(x_j\beta)}-\frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}) + \phi(x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{(\Phi(x_j\beta))^2}+\frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))^2}))\\ \sum_{j=1}^k x_j\phi(x_j\beta)((x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{\Phi(x_j\beta)}-\frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}) + \phi(x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{(\Phi(x_j\beta))^2}+\frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))^2}))
 & \sum_{j=1}^k x_j^2\phi(x_j\beta)((x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{\Phi(x_j\beta)}-\frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}) + \phi(x_j\beta)(\frac{n_j^1}{(\Phi(x_j\beta))^2}+\frac{n_j^0}{(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))^2}))
\end{bmatrix}]$$

$$I(\beta) =\begin{bmatrix} \sum_{j=1}^k n_j\frac{\phi(x_j\beta)^2}{\Phi(x_j\beta)(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}& \sum_{j=1}^k x_jn_j\frac{\phi(x_j\beta)^2}{\Phi(x_j\beta)(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}\\ \sum_{j=1}^k x_jn_j\frac{\phi(x_j\beta)^2}{\Phi(x_j\beta)(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}
 & \sum_{j=1}^k x_j^2n_j\frac{\phi(x_j\beta)^2}{\Phi(x_j\beta)(1-\Phi(x_j\beta))}
\end{bmatrix}$$

### Newton-Raphson Algorithm

#### Recurrence relation for Beta estimation

$$ \beta_{n+1} = \beta_n + (I(\beta_n))^{-1}U(\beta_n), n \ge 1$$

#### Initial values

On procède à une représentation de la fonction de log vraisemblance selon une approche en courbes de niveau puis on sélectionne les valeurs initiales les plus proches des niveaux max.

### Adjustments Tests

#### Deviance D

$$D = 2[L(\beta_{max};n^1) - L(\beta;n^1)] $$

$$L(\beta_{max}; n^1) = \sum_{j=1}^k [log(\binom{n_j}{n_j^1}) + n_j^1log(\frac{n_j^1}{n_j})+n_j^0log(\frac{n_j^0}{n_j})] $$
$$L(\beta; n^1) = \sum_{j=1}^k [log(\binom{n_j}{n_j^1}) + n_j^1log(\pi_j)+n_j^0log(1 - \pi_j)] $$

$$D = 2[\sum_{j=1}^k n_j^1log(\frac{(\frac{n_j^1}{n_j})}{\pi_j})+n_j^0log(\frac{(\frac{n_j^0}{n_j})}{(1-\pi_j)})]$$

#### Pearson Statistics

General Formula:

$$X^2 = \sum_{j=1}^k\frac{(n_j^1 - E(n_j^1))^2}{Var(n_j^1)}$$

$$ \hat{X}^2 = \sum_{j=1}^k \frac{(n_j^1 - n_j\hat{\pi}_j)^2}{n_j\hat{\pi}_j(1-\hat{\pi}_j)} \sim \chi^2_{(k-2)}$$

#### Deviance Residuals (McCullagh, Nedler (1989))

$$\hat{d}_j = sign(n_j^1 - n_j\hat{\pi}_j)\sqrt{2[n_j^1log(\frac{n_j^1}{n_j\hat{\pi}_j})+n_j^0log(\frac{n_j^0}{n_j(1 - \hat{\pi}_j)})]}$$
#### Pearson Residuals

$$\hat{r}_j = \frac{n_j^1 - n_j\hat{\pi}_j}{\sqrt{n_j\hat{\pi}_j(1-\hat{\pi}_j)}}$$
